@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-d-common-source`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-b-property-income`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Builders for the test modules.  No rules of law, no assertions.
--
-- L4 has no record update, so each builder takes every field, with a mixfix
-- segment naming each argument at the call site.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures — builders`

GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item of income from personal exertion`
`a salary of` `the amount` MEANS
    `An item of income from personal exertion` WITH
        `kind`           IS `from employment`
        `taxable amount` IS `the amount`
        `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation` IS FALSE
        `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the kind`   IS A `Kind of income from personal exertion`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
      `first`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `second`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An item of income from personal exertion`
`income of kind` `the kind` `of` `the amount` `; paid for employment income that qualified:` `first` `; qualified in the five years before:` `second` MEANS
    `An item of income from personal exertion` WITH
        `kind`           IS `the kind`
        `taxable amount` IS `the amount`
        `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation` IS `first`
        `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid` IS `second`

-- Version 0.4.0: every field, residence for s 36A included.
GIVEN `the sex`        IS A `Sex`
      `the items`      IS A LIST OF `An item of income from personal exertion`
      `other income`   IS A NUMBER
      `pre-marriage`   IS A NUMBER
      `inherited`      IS A NUMBER
      `claims (a)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims (b)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `widowed`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resident`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`a spouse, with the residence and foreign-worker facts:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` `the items` `; other income` `other income` `; pre-marriage property income` `pre-marriage` `; inherited property income` `inherited` `; claims under (a)` `claims (a)` `; claims under (b)` `claims (b)` `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `section 37` `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `foreign worker` `; an Israeli resident` `resident` MEANS
    `A spouse` WITH
        `sex`                                            IS `the sex`
        `income from personal exertion`                  IS `the items`
        `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS `other income`
        `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage` IS `pre-marriage`
        `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`      IS `inherited`
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS `claims (a)`
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS `claims (b)`
        `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS `widowed`
        `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`        IS `section 37`
        `a foreign worker within the meaning of section 48A`          IS `foreign worker`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year, for section 36A`        IS `resident`

-- Version 0.2.0: every field, the foreign-worker fact of s 48A included.
-- Version 0.4.0: an Israeli resident, as every scenario of 0.1.0-0.3.0 was.
GIVEN `the sex`        IS A `Sex`
      `the items`      IS A LIST OF `An item of income from personal exertion`
      `other income`   IS A NUMBER
      `pre-marriage`   IS A NUMBER
      `inherited`      IS A NUMBER
      `claims (a)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims (b)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `widowed`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `foreign worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`a spouse, with the foreign-worker fact:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` `the items` `; other income` `other income` `; pre-marriage property income` `pre-marriage` `; inherited property income` `inherited` `; claims under (a)` `claims (a)` `; claims under (b)` `claims (b)` `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `section 37` `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `foreign worker` MEANS
    `a spouse, with the residence and foreign-worker facts:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` `the items` `; other income` `other income`
        `; pre-marriage property income` `pre-marriage` `; inherited property income` `inherited`
        `; claims under (a)` `claims (a)` `; claims under (b)` `claims (b)` `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `section 37`
        `; a foreign worker within section 48A` `foreign worker` `; an Israeli resident` TRUE

-- The builder of version 0.1.0, unchanged at the call site: a spouse who is
-- not a foreign worker.  The independent tests (tests-independent.l4) call it.
GIVEN `the sex`        IS A `Sex`
      `the items`      IS A LIST OF `An item of income from personal exertion`
      `other income`   IS A NUMBER
      `pre-marriage`   IS A NUMBER
      `inherited`      IS A NUMBER
      `claims (a)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims (b)`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `widowed`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 37`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`a spouse:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` `the items` `; other income` `other income` `; pre-marriage property income` `pre-marriage` `; inherited property income` `inherited` `; claims under (a)` `claims (a)` `; claims under (b)` `claims (b)` `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `section 37` MEANS
    `a spouse, with the foreign-worker fact:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` `the items` `; other income` `other income`
        `; pre-marriage property income` `pre-marriage` `; inherited property income` `inherited`
        `; claims under (a)` `claims (a)` `; claims under (b)` `claims (b)` `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `section 37`
        `; a foreign worker within section 48A` FALSE

-- A spouse with salary only, nothing else, who may or may not claim.
GIVEN `the sex`   IS A `Sex`
      `salary`    IS A NUMBER
      `claims`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`a salaried spouse:` `the sex` `earning` `salary` `; claims under (a)` `claims` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` `salary`) `; other income` 0
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` `claims` `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

GIVEN `born`        IS A NUMBER
      `of reg`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `of other`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `defers`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `interest`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 66`
`a child born in tax year` `born` `; of the registered spouse` `of reg` `; of the other spouse` `of other` `; mother defers a point` `defers` `; interest` `interest` MEANS
    `A child, for section 66` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                              IS `born`
        `a child of the registered spouse`               IS `of reg`
        `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS `of other`
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS `defers`
        `taxable income from a transparent company`      IS 0
        `taxable income from a real estate investment trust` IS 0
        `taxable income from interest`                   IS `interest`
        `taxable income from capital gain`               IS 0

GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 66`
`a child of both, born in tax year` `born` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` `born` `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 0

GIVEN `the year`   IS A NUMBER
      `registered` IS A `A spouse`
      `other`      IS A `A spouse`
      `kids`       IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 66`
      `source`     IS A MAYBE `A common source of income`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`spouses in tax year` `the year` `; registered` `registered` `; other` `other` `; children` `kids` `; common source` `source` MEANS
    `Spouses in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                    IS `the year`
        `the registered spouse`                       IS `registered`
        `the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS `other`
        `children`                                    IS `kids`
        `common source of income`                     IS `source`
        -- Version 0.4.0: none of the children's (a)(3) income is from
        -- inherited or compensation assets, and this row's readings.
        `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury` IS 0
        `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's` IS NOTHING

-- Version 0.4.0: a couple as given, with the part of the children's (a)(3)
-- income from inherited or compensation assets (fork F6).
GIVEN c IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`the couple` c `, with this much of the children's (a)(3) income from inherited or compensation assets:` p MEANS
    `Spouses in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                    IS c's `tax year`
        `the registered spouse`                       IS c's `the registered spouse`
        `the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS c's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
        `children`                                    IS c's `children`
        `common source of income`                     IS c's `common source of income`
        `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury` IS p
        `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's` IS c's `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's`

-- Version 0.4.0: a couple as given, asked under the readings given.
GIVEN c  IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      rs IS A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`the couple` c `, read as` rs MEANS
    `Spouses in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                    IS c's `tax year`
        `the registered spouse`                       IS c's `the registered spouse`
        `the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS c's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
        `children`                                    IS c's `children`
        `common source of income`                     IS c's `common source of income`
        `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury` IS c's `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury`
        `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's` IS JUST rs

-- Version 0.4.0: this row's readings, each its switch, and the same with one
-- reading named instead.
`this row's readings of section 66` MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS `section 66(d)(1) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails its conditions`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS `section 66(a)(3) — the reading this row takes of the exception in section 65`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS `section 66(a)(2)-(3) — the reading this row takes of the children's income when the pool goes to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS `section 66(b) — the reading this row takes of the proviso as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS `section 66(c)(1A) — the reading this row takes as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS `section 66(c)(1A) — the reading this row takes where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS `section 66(c)(4) — the reading this row takes of section 36A on residence`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 66(d)(1) where a common source of income fails its conditions`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F1 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS r
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) as to the exception in section 65`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F6 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS r
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) where (a)(2) sends the pooled income to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F14 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS r
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the proviso to section 66(b) as to the registered spouse`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F7 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS r
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F18 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS r
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(1A) where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F8 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS r
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS d's `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)`
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of section 36A on residence, for section 66(c)(4)`
GIVETH A `Readings of section 66 for a couple`
`this row's readings, but F20 read as` r MEANS
    `Readings of section 66 for a couple` WITH
        `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)` IS d's `F1, where a common source of income fails subsection (d)(1)`
        `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)` IS d's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`
        `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse` IS d's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`
        `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F7, the proviso to (b) as to the registered spouse`
        `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse` IS d's `F18, (c)(1A) as to the registered spouse`
        `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)` IS d's `F8, (c)(1A) where a common source fails (d)(1)`
        `F20, section 36A and residence, under (c)(4)` IS r
    WHERE d MEANS `this row's readings of section 66`

GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `b1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `b2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `most` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A common source of income`
`a common source: (a)` `a` `; (b) matching` `b1` `; (b) proportional` `b2` `; at home` `home` `; permanent seat` `permanent` `; most activity at home` `most` MEANS
    `A common source of income` WITH
        `the personal exertion of each spouse is required to produce the income` IS `a`
        `each spouse receives income matching his contribution to producing it`  IS `b1`
        `each spouse's income stands in direct proportion to his contribution`   IS `b2`
        `produced in the spouses' residence`                                     IS `home`
        `the residence serves the common source permanently`                     IS `permanent`
        `most of the activity of the source is carried on in the residence`      IS `most`
        -- Version 0.4.0 (fork F1): the facts do not say.
        `the income from personal exertion it gives the spouse who is not the registered spouse, if known` IS NOTHING

-- Version 0.4.0: a common source as given, with the income it gives the
-- spouse who is not the registered spouse (fork F1, reading (ii)).
GIVEN s IS A `A common source of income`
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A common source of income`
`the common source` s `, giving the spouse who is not the registered spouse` x MEANS
    `A common source of income` WITH
        `the personal exertion of each spouse is required to produce the income` IS s's `the personal exertion of each spouse is required to produce the income`
        `each spouse receives income matching his contribution to producing it`  IS s's `each spouse receives income matching his contribution to producing it`
        `each spouse's income stands in direct proportion to his contribution`   IS s's `each spouse's income stands in direct proportion to his contribution`
        `produced in the spouses' residence`                                     IS s's `produced in the spouses' residence`
        `the residence serves the common source permanently`                     IS s's `the residence serves the common source permanently`
        `most of the activity of the source is carried on in the residence`      IS s's `most of the activity of the source is carried on in the residence`
        `the income from personal exertion it gives the spouse who is not the registered spouse, if known` IS JUST x
